{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having epigastric pain and dry heaving for about a week?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that’s right. It’s been really uncomfortable, especially the dry heaving. It’s worse than last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you were admitted just last week for similar symptoms. Can you tell me if anything made it better or worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The IV fluids helped last time. I’ve been trying to keep my G-tube feeds going, but I’ve been nervous about increasing the rate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll start you on IV fluids again to rehydrate you and help settle your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thank you. Is this related to my gastric bypass or the G-tube?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It could be. Given your history, we’re concerned about gastritis or irritation at the gastrojejunal connection. But you’re not showing signs of obstruction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember I had an ulcer there before. Could it be coming back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. We’re not doing an endoscopy this time, but we’ll treat it as if it’s inflammation or mild gastritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be able to keep using my G-tube for feeds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue your G-tube feeds. In fact, we’ve scheduled an enteral infusion for later today at 55 ml/h with full-strength protein."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I was worried I’d have to stop them again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll go slow and monitor you. We’ve also restarted your lansoprazole to reduce stomach acid and help the lining heal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m on rifaximin too—should I keep taking that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re continuing rifaximin. It helps with bacterial overgrowth, which can contribute to your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds—like fluoxetine and aripiprazole? I don’t want to miss doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All your regular medications are being given through the G-tube. We’ve confirmed they’re safe to crush or dissolve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ve also been anxious about these episodes—feels like I’m losing control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s completely understandable. We’re keeping your lorazepam available for anxiety, as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:38:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. What about blood tests? Did they show anything wrong?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs came back normal. White count is fine, no infection. Kidney function and liver enzymes are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No sign of dehydration this time?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You were a bit dehydrated when you arrived, but the IV fluids are correcting that. Your glucose and electrolytes are improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need to be more careful with fluids between feeds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2174-02-10 03:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Small amounts of water or electrolyte solution between feeds can help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2174-02-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2174-02-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better, actually. The nausea has calmed down since the IV fluids started."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2174-02-10 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great. Your vitals are stable, and you’ve had no fever. We’re going to keep the IV fluids running for a few more hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2174-02-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I try increasing the tube feed rate today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2174-02-10 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ve already started the enteral infusion at 55 ml/h. We’ll watch for any discomfort or reflux."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2174-02-10 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve done well with the tube feeds and no symptoms of pain or nausea. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow if this continues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2174-02-10 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Will I need new medications?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2174-02-10 12:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re adding sucralfate four times a day. It coats the stomach and helps heal any irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2174-02-10 12:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How long should I take that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2174-02-10 12:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "For about four weeks. We’ll review it at your follow-up with Dr. Patel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2174-02-10 12:40:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the pain medicine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2174-02-10 12:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll have oxycodone for breakthrough pain, but only if needed. Try the sucralfate and lansoprazole first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2174-02-11 00:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had a good night—no pain, vitals stable. We’re clearing you for discharge this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2174-02-11 00:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Anything I should watch for at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2174-02-11 00:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If nausea or pain returns, slow the feeds and call your doctor. Keep taking sucralfate and your other meds as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2174-02-11 00:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And follow-up is with Dr. Patel?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2174-02-11 00:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, in one week. They’ll assess your progress and adjust treatment if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2174-02-11 00:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you for helping me feel better so quickly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2174-02-11 00:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and don’t hesitate to call if anything changes."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2174-02-10 02:50:00",
    "admission_end": "2174-02-11 12:10:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient was admitted with a one-week history of dry heaving and epigastric pain, recurring shortly after a prior hospitalization for similar symptoms. She has a complex surgical history including Roux-en-Y gastric bypass and gastrostomy tube placement due to prior GJ anastomotic ulcer. On admission, she was started on IV fluids, which resolved her symptoms. She remained hemodynamically stable, afebrile, and without leukocytosis. Laboratory results were largely normal, and she tolerated enteral nutrition via G-tube at full strength. Treatment included continuation of lansoprazole and rifaximin, with addition of sucralfate for gastric protection. She was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to continue medications and follow up with her specialist.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified gastritis and gastroduodenitis, without mention of hemorrhage",
      "Bariatric surgery status",
      "Gastrostomy status",
      "Personal history of peptic ulcer disease",
      "Polycystic ovaries",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other chronic nonalcoholic liver disease",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
